An idea I had: It should be possible to (a)pply a bladed weapon towards a 
corpse and chop the corpse into pieces. For instance, you could chop up
a unicorn and get a unicorn a unicorn head, a unicorn horn, a unicorn heart,
several pieces of unicorn meat (which would be food but would spoil) and 
some unicorn bones. This would allow large monsters that are too heavy to
move to be sacrificed (I would assume that a God would be perfectly happy
if you just sacrificed the heart. Its not like a God actually wants the 
corpse... its the thought that counts.) Also, there are a lot of monsters
who have interesting body parts. Umber hulk claws could be used to dig. 
Dragon scales and Unicorn horns and worm teeth already exist of course. 
Maybe if you kill a troll and chop it up and get its heart and bless it, 
the heart would generate a new troll, but it would be tame. (Of course,
if you cho pa troll up, every piece of troll would generate a new troll,
so this strategy, while yielding a pet troll, would be dangerous). 
A medusa head would be a good wepaon (as someone else pointed out).
There should be a rabbit that you could kill, and get a rabbits foot which
would act like a luckstone. 

Another thought I had is that (q)uaffing potions should leave empty potion
bottles behind, which could be filled with water to make potions of water, or
which could be used to catch the blood from a sliced up corpse (see above).
Different blood would have different uses. A potion of cockatrice blood, if
thrown, would turn someone to stone. A potion of yellow dragon blood would
be very powerful acid which would turn whatever it was thrown at to stone.
A potion of gray dragon blood would be so magical that wands dipped in it
would be recharged. Etc.

